TITLE:: RLChordSpace
summary:: A pitch system and the chord types allowed in it
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLChord, Classes/RLChordContext, Classes/RLPitchSystem, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
A chord space is a link::Classes/RLPitchSystem:: and a list of chord strong::types::. A type is a name and a strong::pattern::, the pitch-class intervals of its tones above the root, root first. The chords of the space are link::Classes/RLChord::s, a root and a type each.

link::#*triads:: builds the usual space of a system: the triad nearest 4:5:6 and its inversion.

table::
## major || code::[0, a, b]:: || a the system's 5/4, b its 3/2
## minor || code::[0, b - a, b]:: || the same intervals upside down
::

A space is a value: equal to another with the same system and types.

code::
~space = RLChordSpace.triads(RLEDO(12));
~space.pattern(\minor);            // [0, 3, 7]
~space.major(0).pcs;               // [0, 4, 7]
~space.find([9, 0, 4]);            // A minor
~space.all.size;                   // 24

RLChordSpace.triads(RLEDO(19)).pattern(\major);       // [0, 6, 11]
RLChordSpace.triads(RLJust([3, 5])).minor.pcs;        // [[0, 0], [1, -1], [1, 0]]: 1/1, 6/5, 3/2
RLChordSpace.triads(RLEDO(22), [9, 7], [3, 2]).pattern(\major);   // [0, 8, 13]: a triad on the supermajor third
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: system
argument:: types
An Array of code::[name, pattern]:: pairs.

METHOD:: triads
The triad nearest strong::third:: and strong::fifth:: above a root, named code::\major::, and its inversion, code::\minor::.
argument:: system
argument:: third
A just ratio, 5/4 by default.
argument:: fifth
3/2 by default.

METHOD:: pair
A chord type and the same turned upside down between its root and its top tone: what an link::Classes/RLChordContext:: asks for, with chords of any size.
argument:: system
argument:: name
argument:: pattern
The pitch classes of the first type above its root, root first.
argument:: inverseName

METHOD:: tetrads
The tetrad nearest 4:5:6:7, named code::\otonal::, and its inversion, code::\utonal::: in 12 steps a dominant seventh code::[0, 4, 7, 10]:: and a half-diminished seventh code::[0, 3, 6, 10]::; on code::RLJust([3, 5, 7]):: 1/1, 5/4, 3/2, 7/4 and 1/1, 7/6, 7/5, 7/4. A lattice without the prime 7 is an Error.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: system
METHOD:: types

METHOD:: otonal
METHOD:: utonal
The chord of that type on a root (the origin when none is given), in a space of tetrads.

METHOD:: typeNames
METHOD:: typeIndex
METHOD:: typeAt
The names of the types, the index of a name, the name at an index.

METHOD:: pattern
The pattern of a type. An unknown name is an Error.

METHOD:: chord
The chord of a root and a type (the first type when none is given).

METHOD:: major
METHOD:: minor
The chord of that type on a root (the origin when none is given).

METHOD:: all
Every chord of a finite system, type by type. An Error on the lattice.

METHOD:: canonical
A symmetric chord has several roots (C, E and Ab augmented are one chord in 12 steps): the chord of the same type and tones on the first of them.

METHOD:: distinct
Every chord of a finite system once: 28 for major, minor and augmented triads in 12 steps, where link::#-all:: has 36.

METHOD:: find
The chord with these pitch classes, in any order, or nil.
